Subject: [PATCH 1/3] A setting changed by chat is not also saved as a memory
 (CR-0051)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Real-AI run 30 (main 04f01dd, Claude CLI), U17: "Switch to dark mode"
changed the theme with "Changed: Theme → Dark. Undo", and the post-turn
review also saved "Prefers dark mode"; Undo of the theme left the fact.
The words were an instruction to foo that the setting line records, so a
message whose intake kind was `setting` is now left out of the review
(08-3 §12.4 Input, X-209). Later messages are reviewed as before.

Fidelity-CR: CR-0051

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
